</subtitle><entry><title type="html">Semantic Detour Flow</title><link href="https://quandao10.github.io/blog/2026/semantic-detour-flow/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Semantic Detour Flow" /><published>2026-11-23T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-11-23T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://quandao10.github.io/blog/2026/semantic-detour-flow</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://quandao10.github.io/blog/2026/semantic-detour-flow/"><![CDATA[<p>Diffusion models trained in semantic latent spaces converge much faster than pixel-space
models, but they inherit a decoder that caps fine detail. <strong>Semantic Detour Flow</strong> closes most
of that gap without any decoder: it is a pixel-space flow that follows frozen DINOv2 features
at high noise and hands over to pixels at low noise. One network, one velocity loss, and
sampling that runs entirely in pixel space.</p>

